  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday Night through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1004 AM CST Wed Nov 25 2026\n\nExpected snowfall amounts remain in flux, but the potential is\ndefinitely there for significant (1\"+) accumulations tomorrow\nnight through early Friday, mainly for the Cumberland Plateau.\nA few other spots could see lighter accumulations, but the primary\nfocus is the Cumberland Plateau. Temperatures on Friday will be\nseveral degrees above freezing, so whatever snow does accumulate \nlikely won't remain on the ground for long. Meanwhile, \ntemperatures Friday night look to be especially frigid, with \nwidespread readings in the 20s and perhaps even a few teens in the\ncolder spots. Temperatures on Saturday will recover nicely as a \nsurface ridge slides across the region, but the next active \nweather system will being additional rain chances to the mid state\non Sunday. Looking ahead, rain chances will drop off considerably\nafter Sunday, with mild temperatures expected throughout next \nweek.",
